pouch boundary-line patch 0030 - fopen("a") / O_APPEND seek-to-END.

WHY THIS PATCH EXISTS (the gfx-4 merge decision, made honest).

The aux track's 0024-pouch-fopen-create was DROPPED at the gfx-4 -> main
merge as subsumed: main's 0023-pouch-fopen already routes fopen/tmpfile
through the public open(), and main's 0024-pouch-fs-process-wires carries
the same O_CREAT -> SYS_WALK_CREATE arm and the same O_TRUNC -> OTRUNC
mapping. That reading was correct for those two arms.

It was NOT correct for O_APPEND, which the dropped patch also carried and
main's 0024 does not. The merge kept usr/pouch-hello/pouch-hello-fopen.c
precisely as the regression that would hold the subsumption claim honest,
and on the first post-merge boot it did exactly that:

    pouch-hello-fopen: create OK
    pouch-hello-fopen: FAIL append line1 (errno 38)

i.e. fopen("a") + fputs("beta") overwrote "alpha" at offset 0 instead of
extending the file. (The errno 38/ENOSYS in that line is incidental -- it
is the stale errno left by the no-op fcntl below; the actual failure is
the read-back content mismatch.)

MECHANISM. Thylacine has no kernel append mode: an fd carries a plain
cursor and SYS_WALK_OPEN has no O_APPEND-equivalent omode bit. musl's
__fdopen handles append by asking the kernel for it --

    if (*mode == 'a') {
        int flags = __syscall(SYS_fcntl, fd, F_GETFL);
        if (!(flags & O_APPEND))
            __syscall(SYS_fcntl, fd, F_SETFL, flags | O_APPEND);
        f->flags |= F_APP;
    }

-- and pouch answers F_SETFL with ENOSYS. So nothing positions the cursor
and every append write lands at offset 0, clobbering the file.

FIX. Seek to END once, at open, for any successful open carrying O_APPEND.

Applied through a single helper (pouch_open_ret) rather than at one return
site, because openat() has THREE successful-open exits -- create-ok,
EEXIST-fallback-open, and plain-open -- and a per-site fix would silently
miss one. (That is not hypothetical: the CL-4 audit's F2 was exactly this
shape, a console fstat fix that covered one of two front doors.) The two
remaining __syscall_ret sites are provably negative-only: one guards
p < 0, the other is reached only when r < 0 and is not the EEXIST case.

SEMANTICS, stated honestly. This makes SINGLE-WRITER append correct -- the
config-file / log-file case fopen("a") is actually used for. CONCURRENT
appenders may still interleave, because the seek and the write are not
atomic. That atomicity is documented-ABSENT, not silently claimed; closing
it needs a real kernel append mode (a v1.x SYS_WALK_OPEN omode bit), at
which point this seek becomes redundant and should be removed with it.

SYS_lseek is wired 1:1 to the kernel's SYS_LSEEK (= 51) by patch 0010
(arch/aarch64/bits/syscall.h.in redefines __NR_lseek 0xFFFF -> 51).

Files: src/fcntl/openat.c (one helper + three call-site retargets).
Regression: usr/pouch-hello/pouch-hello-fopen.c "append" leg, boot-fatal
via joey's #50 probe.

--- a/src/fcntl/openat.c	2026-07-30 09:00:00
+++ b/src/fcntl/openat.c	2026-07-30 09:00:00
@@ -22,12 +22,34 @@
 #include <errno.h>
 #include <stddef.h>
 #include <string.h>
+#include <unistd.h>
 #include "syscall.h"
 #include "_pouch_fs.h"
 
 /* SYS_open +OTRUNC (SYS_WALK_OPEN_OMODE_VALID includes OTRUNC = 0x10). */
 #define POUCH_OTRUNC  0x10u
 
+/* O_APPEND (patch 0030). Thylacine has NO kernel append mode: an fd carries a
+ * plain cursor, and musl's __fdopen tries fcntl(F_SETFL, O_APPEND) -- which
+ * pouch answers ENOSYS -- so nothing positions the cursor. Without this seek
+ * fopen("a") writes at offset 0 and CLOBBERS the file it meant to extend.
+ *
+ * Applied HERE, at a single helper every successful-open exit routes through,
+ * rather than at one return site: openat() has three such exits (create-ok,
+ * EEXIST-fallback-open, plain-open) and a per-site fix would silently miss
+ * one. Error exits pass negatives through untouched.
+ *
+ * Single-writer append is thereby correct (the config-file / log-file case
+ * fopen("a") is actually used for). CONCURRENT appenders may interleave --
+ * that atomicity is documented-ABSENT, not silently claimed; it needs a real
+ * kernel append mode (a v1.x SYS_WALK_OPEN omode bit). */
+static int pouch_open_ret(long r, int flags)
+{
+	if (r >= 0 && (flags & O_APPEND))
+		__syscall(SYS_lseek, r, 0, SEEK_END);
+	return __syscall_ret(r);
+}
+
 int openat(int fd, const char *filename, int flags, ...)
 {
 	mode_t mode = 0;
@@ -77,7 +99,7 @@
 
 		long r = __syscall(SYS_thyla_walk_create, p, leaf, llen,
 		                   omode, (unsigned)mode & 0777u);
-		if (r >= 0) { __syscall(SYS_close, p); return __syscall_ret(r); }
+		if (r >= 0) { __syscall(SYS_close, p); return pouch_open_ret(r, flags); }
 
 		/* Exists + no O_EXCL: open the existing file (+OTRUNC on O_TRUNC).
 		 * Any other create error propagates. */
@@ -85,7 +107,7 @@
 			unsigned long om = omode | ((flags & O_TRUNC) ? POUCH_OTRUNC : 0u);
 			long o = __syscall(SYS_thyla_open, (long)p, leaf, llen, om);
 			__syscall(SYS_close, p);
-			return __syscall_ret(o);
+			return pouch_open_ret(o, flags);
 		}
 		__syscall(SYS_close, p);
 		return __syscall_ret(r);
@@ -94,6 +116,6 @@
 	/* Non-create open: one stalk-resolved open from the Territory root
 	 * (relative paths cwd-join via the FROM_ROOT arm). O_TRUNC -> +OTRUNC. */
 	unsigned long om = omode | ((flags & O_TRUNC) ? POUCH_OTRUNC : 0u);
-	return __syscall_ret(__syscall(SYS_thyla_open, POUCH_FROM_ROOT,
-	                               filename, len, om));
+	return pouch_open_ret(__syscall(SYS_thyla_open, POUCH_FROM_ROOT,
+	                                filename, len, om), flags);
 }
